From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] diffkv attention: split-KV (3D) launch for MTP verification

VLLM_MIMO26_DIFFKV_SPEC_3D=1 (default 0 = unchanged; on in profile default).
The TRITON_ATTN_DIFFKV launcher takes the split-KV 3D kernel only for
max_seqlen_q == 1, so MTP verification (1 + k query tokens per request) runs
the 2D kernel: with MiMo's GQA 16 that is one program per (query token, kv
head) walking the whole KV prefix, a few programs on 104 SMs. Verify steps on
full-attention layers now also use the 3D kernel when 1 < max_seqlen_q <= 16,
the batch has at most seq_threshold_3D sequences and its tokens fit the
preallocated segment buffers. The 3D kernel and its reduction already store
and combine partials per query token. The choice depends only on the batch
shape, so each CUDA graph captures one fixed path. Sliding-window layers are
left on the 2D kernel (their 128-token window gains nothing).

One global layer (64 q / 4 kv heads, qk 192, v 128), c1 with 4 query tokens:
8k 0.62 -> 0.21 ms, 55k 3.70 -> 0.88, 134k 7.79 -> 1.62, 268k 14.29 -> 3.20;
c8 (32 tokens) 55k 4.38 -> 3.95. Outputs differ from the 2D kernel at
rounding level (max |diff| <= 4.9e-4), always finite.
---
diff --git a/vllm/mimo26_opt_profile.py b/vllm/mimo26_opt_profile.py
index f6fea83..6072e78 100644
--- a/vllm/mimo26_opt_profile.py
+++ b/vllm/mimo26_opt_profile.py
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@ PROFILES: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {
         # dim split 128 + 64 instead of padding to 256 (bitwise equal)
         "VLLM_MIMO26_DIFFKV_PREFILL_BM": "128",
         "VLLM_MIMO26_DIFFKV_QK_SPLIT": "1",
+        # 0011 MTP verification on full-attention layers uses split-KV (3D)
+        # attention (c1 at 55k context: 3.7 -> 0.9 ms per global layer)
+        "VLLM_MIMO26_DIFFKV_SPEC_3D": "1",
     },
 }
 
diff --git a/vllm/v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention_diffkv.py b/vllm/v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention_diffkv.py
index 2bbb1bc..bd53b78 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention_diffkv.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention_diffkv.py
@@ -510,6 +510,30 @@ def unified_attention_diffkv(
         or num_seqs > seq_threshold_3D
         or is_batch_invariant
     )
+    # VLLM_MIMO26_DIFFKV_SPEC_3D=1 (default 0 = unchanged): MTP verification
+    # launches (1 < max_seqlen_q <= 16 query tokens per sequence) also use the
+    # split-KV 3D kernel when the batch fits the preallocated segment buffers.
+    # The 2D kernel gives each (query token, kv head) ONE program that walks
+    # the whole KV prefix, so a c1 verify step over a long context runs on a
+    # handful of SMs; the 3D kernel and its reduction already index partials
+    # per query token. The path depends only on the batch shape, so every
+    # CUDA graph captures one fixed path. Full-attention layers only: the
+    # sliding-window (128) layers read a short window either way.
+    if (
+        not use_3d
+        and window_size[0] < 0
+        and os.environ.get("VLLM_MIMO26_DIFFKV_SPEC_3D", "0") == "1"
+        and 1 < max_seqlen_q <= 16
+        and softmax_segm_output is not None
+        and softmax_segm_max is not None
+        and softmax_segm_expsum is not None
+        and num_par_softmax_segments is not None
+        and seq_threshold_3D is not None
+        and num_seqs <= seq_threshold_3D
+        and q.shape[0] <= softmax_segm_output.shape[0]
+        and not is_batch_invariant
+    ):
+        use_3d = True
 
     # Tile size: 32 for prefill-class kernels.  Decode (small Q) prefers
     # smaller tiles to expose more parallelism along the KV dim.
